WEBVTT

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.000
(SNORING)

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.560
Klaus. Klaus, the pinata's drooping.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.240
(SNORING)

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.200
Hand me the ratchet wrench.
I can fix it. Ow!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.080
Hey, Marlin?

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.680
(MARLIN SNORING)

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.640
Oh. Hey, guys, I was just--

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.720
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.040
Dory! It's not time to get up yet.
You have to go back to bed.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.360
And remember, the anemone stings.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.800
Oh right. Yeah. Sorry.
Back to bed, back to bed.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.720
Hey, Marlin? Ow!

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.360
Back to bed! That was it.
Very simple. Bed. Back to it.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.480
DORY: Mmm, got it.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:57.960
Hey, Marlin?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.280
And we're up. That's it.
Ready to start the day.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.560
-And we were looking for something.
-Nemo.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.080
Right. I remember it
like it was yesterday.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.080
Of course, I don't really remember
yesterday all that well.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.200
(NEMO LAUGHING)

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.160
Anyway, I would say the scariest
moment of the trip was the 4 sharks.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.040
NEMO: Wait, I thought
there were 3 sharks.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.560
MARLIN: No. No,
there were definitely four.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.160
But last time you told it,
there were three.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.720
Son, which one of us traveled
across the entire ocean?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.440
-Nemo did.
-(YELPS)

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.240
Obviously we had to cross the ocean...

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.320
to find him, so you know... He went first.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.760
I guess that's true. Isn't it?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.120
Well, you made it!
You almost missed the field trip.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.760
A field trip? Ooh, I love field trips.
Where are we going?

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.920
-I thought you told her.
-I did tell her!

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.760
-Uh... Dory.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:50.080
Mr. Ray has too many fish
to keep an eye on today.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.280
Uh-huh.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.040
So it would be best if today
you weren't exactly with the class.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.240
Oh. Why not?

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.480
Well, you know, you have problems
remembering things sometimes.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.360
That's the one thing I can remember.
Yes.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.480
Okay. And sometimes it's not your fault,
but it can cause you to wander.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.680
And Mr. Ray doesn't really have time
to worry about fish who wander.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.680
In other words,
he doesn't have enough help.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.280
Poor guy.
You know, he's so overworked.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.880
-You understand.
-I totally understand now.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:19.440
-Okay.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.880
He wants me
to be the teacher's assistant.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.080
Uh... No, not exactly.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.120
I am so honored. I have never been
a teaching assistant before.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.640
Mr. Ray! You got help.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.800
(LAUGHS AWKWARDLY)
Oh. Okeydokey.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.760
(STUDENTS LAUGHING)

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.640
-All right, kids.
-All right, kids.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.240
-Today's the day!
-Today's the day!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.000
Our field trip to the sting ray migration.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:43.920
Sting ray migration.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.160
Now, does anyone know
why we migrate?

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:47.920
(COUGHS)

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.360
Come on. You got to know this stuff.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.280
Migration is about going back to...

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.440
-Bed!
-Yes!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.320
-No.
-No.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.480
-The sand!
-No! Migration is about going home.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.160
-Home.
-Which is where you're from.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.000
Where you're from.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.240
Can someone tell me
where they're from?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.680
-I live by a giant rock.
-I live 3 coral caves away from here.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.360
My house is covered in algae.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.840
Where'd you grow up, Dory?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Me? Um, I don't know.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.040
My family. Where are they?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.200
-Can I help you?
-(STUDENTS LAUGHING)

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.960
I'm sorry. Did I forget again?
You see, I suffer from--

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.680
STUDENTS: Short-term memory loss.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.440
How can you remember your family
if you have short-term memory loss?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.080
Good question. See, I can remember
some things because well...

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.880
They make sense.
Like, um, I have a family.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.480
I know because I've-- I must have
come from somewhere. Right?

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.720
Everyone has a family.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.080
I may not remember their names
and what they look like.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.440
And I may not even be able to
ever find them again, but, um...

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.800
-What were we talking about?
-Mommies and daddies.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.560
Mommies and daddies. Right.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:54.560
Why are we talking about
mommies and daddies? Oh. Oh!

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.440
That class. Uh-oh. Why me? Okay.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.400
You guys seem a little young,
but, um, okay.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.240
You see, kids,
when two fish love each other--

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.600
And we'll stop right there.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.920
Climb aboard, explorers.
I feel a migration song coming on.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.600
Oh...

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.240
♪ Migration, migration
let's learn about migration

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.240
♪ It's nature's inspiration
to move around the sea

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.320
♪ Here's a scientific promise
That a fish who's Oceanodromous

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.440
♪ Where did everyone go? I'm by myself
Oh there they are. I'm back

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.640
♪ Plus or minus 4 degrees
based on solar positioning ♪

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.480
Oh, kids stay away from the edge.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.760
Okay, you hear that? Okay, everybody
stay back from the edge. Come on.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.600
-Okay, that's too far.
-That's too far.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.680
Come on. Come on.
Get back over here. Back this way.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.920
-Now, I need everyone to listen to me.
-All right, listen up!

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.600
-When the rays pass through here--
-The rays, gonna pass through.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.440
What do we have to be careful of?

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.120
Everybody has to be careful of what?
Hmm?

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.600
ALL: The undertow!
MR. RAY: That's right.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.320
That's right. The under-- The undertow?

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:03.280
MR. RAY: Because the current created
by all the flapping is very strong.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.640
And if you're not careful,
you can get pulled into--

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.840
Mr. Ray! So how do the stingrays
all know where to go?

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.120
That's what an instinct is, Nemo.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.480
Something deep inside you that feels
so familiar that you have to listen to it.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:21.400
Like a song you've always known.
And I can hear mine now!

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.800
STINGRAYS: ♪ To and fro,
our hearts know where to go

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.800
♪ Beating like a drum
it sends us back to where we're from

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.160
♪ Oh... we're going home

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.560
-♪ We know who we are...
-(STUDENTS GASPING)

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.840
♪ And it's time to travel far

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.840
♪ For days and nights we'll roam,
to make our way back home

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.800
♪ Oh... we're going home

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.080
-♪ Swimming to and fro,
-Wow!

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.000
♪ Our hearts know where to go

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.240
♪ Beating like a drum, it sends us back
to where we're from ♪

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:52.120
We see the undertow
and we say-- (SCREAMS)

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.240
-ALL: Dory!
-(SCREAMING)

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.360
Dory!

00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.640
MR. RAY: Dory! Dory!

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.360
-(GASPS) Is she dead?
-MR. RAY: No, she's not dead.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.840
-STUDENTS: Aw. Oh man.
-Give her some space, everybody.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.960
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.680
The Jewel of Morro Bay, California?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.520
I remembered something so I--

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.800
(GASPS) I remembered something!

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.480
I actually remembered something!
Something important.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.600
Something important?
What? What was it?

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.520
Uh... I'm not sure anymore,
but I can still feel it. It's right there.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.200
All right, thank you, Mr. Ray.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.800
Okay, come on. Try to remember better.
Don't be such a Dory, Dory.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.760
Hmm. I don't know. I-- Hold on. Hold on.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.000
-Uh... Oh. Oh!
-What? Did you remember?

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.560
Ugh, I don't remember.
It was something-- It was--

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:42.800
Oh, oh, oh! It was something about the--

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.880
-The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
-(GASPS)

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.080
My family!
(GASPS) I remember my family!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.080
They're out there somewhere.
I have to find them.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.720
Guys, you got to help me.
Guys! Guys! Hello?

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.840
Guys! Where are you?

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.240
-MARLIN: Dory!
-Hello?

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.760
-Dory!
-Ah! Where did you go?

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.080
-You were the one to go.
-My parents. I remembered them.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.680
What? What did you remember?

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.920
I remembered them! My mom. My dad.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.920
I have a family. Oh! They don't know
where I am. Let's go. We have to go.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.520
Dory, no. No! This is crazy!
Where exactly are you trying to go?

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.120
To the Gem of the Baltic?

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.640
-The Jewel of Morro Bay, California.
-Yes!

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.880
No, Dory. California's all the way
across the ocean.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.000
Then we'd better get going.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.920
How come every time we're on the edge
of this reef, one of us is trying...

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.760
to leave?
For once, can't we just enjoy the view?

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.520
How can you be talking about the view
when I remembered my family?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.840
No! We've done our ocean travels.
That part of our lives is over.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.280
The only reason to travel
in the first place is so...

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.600
-you don't have to travel ever again.
-Yeah, but I want to--

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:43.960
(MARLIN GROANS AND COUGHS)

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.920
-Dory, look--
-Please.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.440
All I know is that I miss them.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.880
I really, really miss them.
I didn't know what that felt like.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.640
Do you know what that feels like?

